      "math_academy_id": "q-74123",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Given the vectors $a=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(a,b).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(a,b) & =‖a-b‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({a}_{1}-{b}_{1})^{2}+({a}_{2}-{b}_{2})^{2}+({a}_{3}-{b}_{3})^{2}+({a}_{4}-{b}_{4})^{2}+({a}_{5}-{b}_{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5-3)^{2}+(3-5)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}+(1-(-1))^{2}+(6-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+4+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
